{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the children struggled.</b> From the root מרוצה, the tzadi is doubled, and its cognate \"like lightning flashes they race\" (Nahum 2:5). They are called children on account of their end, and likewise \"and you strip the naked of their garments\" (Job 22:6). And it is a question to women who have given birth: if such a thing has happened to them, and they say no:" "<b>And the sense of \"If so, why am I thus.\"</b> The thing and the custom — why is my pregnancy different:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Resolved והצדי\"ק as referring to the letter tzadi in ויתרוצצו being doubled (with dagesh); reading follows the standard grammatical interpretation."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:48.236984332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}